From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:08:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0026] page: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: the page robot hook
 (FEF_PAGEBOT)

The Randomizer page reports where it drew each control this frame
(RandoPage::targets: btn:start, btn:everything_on, btn:defaults,
btn:back, btn:original, btn:random, row:<key>, opt:<key>=<value>) and
the background makes it threw away (RandoPage::thrown), and offers
values_text() (the exact text Start game sends), has_rows() and
rows_settled(). Nothing else on the page changes.

New pagebot.rs: with FEF_PAGEBOT=<script.json> and
FEF_PAGEBOT_LOG=<file> in a --headless run of Fire Emblem Fates, the
mode pick waits for the page as it does with a window (the game does
not run while the page is open), the real page is drawn each frame
into an egui context that has no window, and the script's clicks are
real pointer events at the rectangles the page reported (a click goes
out only at a rectangle that stayed the same for two frames). One JSON
line per event in the log (hook, page_open, prebuild_start,
prebuild_done, discarded, click, expect, answer, laid, avatar, end).
The run ends by itself when the script is done, or after 10 minutes
with the page open. The headless pace (FEF_HEADLESS_PACE) does not
count the time the page was open.

Without FEF_PAGEBOT nothing runs: run_headless and rando() take the old
path (round 61: the headless memory hashes of a run with the randomizer
off are identical to the round-60 exe's at frames 0, 3000, 4600, 5200).
Tools: tools/harness/pagebot.py, docs/tests/PAGEBOT.md.
